    <briefdescription>
<para>Memory allocation failure error. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para><ref refid="classcslt_1_1BadAllocError" kindref="compound">BadAllocError</ref> represents an error when malloc, calloc, or new fails to allocate memory.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="par"><title>Example Usage:</title><para><programlisting><codeline><highlight class="normal">throw<sp/>BadAllocError();<sp/><sp/>//<sp/>&quot;Memory<sp/>allocation<sp/>failed&quot;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">throw<sp/>BadAllocError(&quot;Failed<sp/>to<sp/>allocate<sp/>1024<sp/>bytes<sp/>for<sp/>buffer&quot;);</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting> </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
